  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ are placed in a circle in such a way that for each valid iii, AiA_iAi​ and Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ are adjacent, and A1A_1A1​ and ANA_NAN​ are also adjacent.\n\nWe want to repeat the following operation exactly N−1N-1N−1 times (until only one number remains):\n\n\nSelect two adjacent numbers. Let's denote them by aaa and bbb.\nScore a+ba+ba+b penalty points.\nErase both aaa and bbb from the circle and insert a+ba+ba+b in the space between them.\nWhat is the minimum number of penalty points we can score?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "2≤N≤4002 \\le N \\le 4002≤N≤400",
      "1≤ai≤1091 \\le a_i \\le 10^91≤ai​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):**",
      "2≤N≤102 \\le N \\le 102≤N≤10",
      "ai≤10a_i \\le 10ai​≤10 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #2 (10 points):**",
      "2≤N≤252 \\le N \\le 252≤N≤25",
      "a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​ are distinct powers of 222 (including 111)",
      "**Subtask #3 (10 points):** 2≤N≤1002 \\le N \\le 1002≤N≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the minimum number of penalty points.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n3\n10 10 1",
        "output": "32",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\n[10,10,1]→[10,11][10,10,1] \\rightarrow [10, 11][10,10,1]→[10,11], penalty:  111111\n[10,11]→[21][10,11] \\rightarrow [21][10,11]→[21], penalty:  212121\nTotal penalty: 11+21=3211+21=3211+21=32"
      }
    ]
  },
